ed archive PR #7520 (task 14197, issue #7297): re-applies the PR's only unique remainder onto current main. PR #7520 is not reopened and its deleted archive branch is not recreated; the closed PR stays the preservation record.\n\nFresh revalidation base: `origin/main` `6f30e9c0f1`. Branch merged current `origin/main` (`1cdf70c78c`) before this PR opened.\n\nContent-level verification: PR #7520's diff vs its merge-base added exactly 63 lines, all in `pkgs/id/tests/probe_attestation_sign.rs` — a file absent from `origin/main`. The probe pins the behaviour it asked about: `sign_genesis` / `sign_claim` do not refuse a signer who is not one of the agreement's two players, and `compute_state` ignores non-player genesis and claims (state stays `Proposed`). It also pins the existing duplicate-seat refusal (#2863 precedent).\n\nAdaptation to sibling convention (as in the #7550 currency-probe salvage, PR #7947 lineage): the archived `//` header became a `//!` module doc (clears the `missing-docs` warning the archived form raised), diagnostic `println!` lines became assertions on the same observed values, and the file is rustfmt-clean under edition 2024 — no semantic change.\n\nTests: `cargo test -p id --test probe_attestation_sign` on the laptop (amd) — 1 passed, 0 failed. CI runs the target through the shards automatically (`tests/*.rs` are globbed at run time).\n\nRefs #7297.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796795646&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7979&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7979&signature=c30812114e1a9db626d563b0bde0b9fe2dcf3e026476f87be189a445bd992a7e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.black